course: dictionary
lesson: 751
title: One word, many battles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Battle has more than one meaning, so read the words around it to find the right one. «Vikings did not wear horned helmets in battle» means a fight between armies, because the sentence is about warriors and helmets.
explain: Battle can also mean any hard struggle or contest. In «the battle is over», the sentence tells you it is about a game: you respect the game and the effort, win or lose. Here battle means a contest, not a war.
explain: Battle can also be a verb: to battle is to fight or try very hard against something difficult. Test it by swapping in a meaning. If «fight or try very hard against» fits the sentence and still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A battle is a fight between armies, ships or planes in a war.
fact: A battle can also be any hard struggle or contest, like a battle of the bands.
fact: To battle means to fight or try very hard against something difficult.
fact: In 1066 William of Normandy won the Battle of Hastings, where King Harold died, and became king of England.
fact: Useful phrases: fight a battle, uphill battle, losing battle, battle it out.
exercise: «In 1066 William of Normandy won the Battle of Hastings.» What kind of battle is this? | *A fight between armies in a war | A hard maths test | A long walk in the rain | Like a game of chess
exercise: Mia says, «Every night I have a battle with my maths homework.» What does battle mean here? | A ship at sea | *A hard struggle against something difficult | A football match | A fight with swords
exercise: «The team had to battle through the rain to finish the race.» What does battle mean? | To sing loudly | To sit down and rest | *To fight or try very hard against something difficult | To sleep late
test: Which meaning fits «an uphill battle against illness»? | A sleepy afternoon | A game of football | *A long, hard struggle | A steep walk up a hill
test: Which word is a synonym for battle, meaning a fight in a war? | Sleep | Picnic | *Conflict | Lunch
exam: «The handshake line is a signal that the battle is over.» Battle here means: | A war between two countries | *A contest or game | A sword fight | A ship at sea
